@host = http://localhost:5225

### Sign in. Returns 204 and two HttpOnly cookies; no token in the body.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dev@regos.local",
  "password": "development-password"
}

### Who am I? Authenticated by the access cookie the request above set.
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### Renew the session. Rotates the refresh token: the old one dies here.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh

### Sign out. Revokes the refresh token and clears both cookies.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout

### Now unauthenticated -> 401.
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### Presenting the rotated refresh token again ends every session for the user.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
Cookie: regos_refresh=a-token-that-was-never-issued

### Every failed sign-in returns one status and one message (ADR-022).
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dev@regos.local",
  "password": "wrong"
}
